### `vsplotter`

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| `id` | `vsplotter` |
| `kind` | `sedea-extension` |
| `extensionId` | `RafaelArvelo.vsplotter` |
| `installVersion` | `1.9.0` |
| `minVersion` | `1.9.0` |
| `docsUrl` | https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=RafaelArvelo.vsplotter |
| `installUrl` | https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/_apis/public/gallery/publishers/RafaelArvelo/vsextensions/vsplotter/1.9.0/vspackage |
| `macosMethods` | `marketplace-vsix-sedea-cli` |
| `linuxMethods` | `marketplace-vsix-sedea-cli` |
| `windowsMethods` | `marketplace-vsix-sedea-cli` |

Probe and dry-run:

```text
"<sedea-cli>" --list-extensions --show-versions
```

Match `RafaelArvelo.vsplotter` case-insensitively and require version ≥ `1.9.0`.
Sedea's configured Open VSX gallery does not contain this extension. Therefore
`marketplace-vsix-sedea-cli` is the sole installation method: download the
pinned VSIX from the official Microsoft Visual Studio Marketplace URL in this
registry, then install that local file with the resolved Sedea CLI. Do not try
an extension-id gallery install, ask the user to locate a VSIX, use a third-party
downloader, substitute another plotting extension, or install into another
editor.

## Sedea CLI resolution

| OS | Resolution |
|----|------------|
| macOS | `/Applications/Sedea.app/Contents/Resources/app/bin/code` |
| Linux | `sedea` on PATH, or user-supplied Sedea CLI |
| Windows | `sedea` on PATH, or user-supplied Sedea CLI |

Install after consent on macOS or Linux:

```bash
tmp_dir="$(mktemp -d)"
vsix="$tmp_dir/RafaelArvelo.vsplotter-1.9.0.vsix"
curl -fsSL --compressed \
  -o "$vsix" \
  "https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/_apis/public/gallery/publishers/RafaelArvelo/vsextensions/vsplotter/1.9.0/vspackage"
"<sedea-cli>" --install-extension "$vsix" --force
rm -rf "$tmp_dir"
```

Install after consent on Windows PowerShell:

```powershell
$vsix = Join-Path $env:TEMP "RafaelArvelo.vsplotter-1.9.0.vsix"
Invoke-WebRequest `
  -Uri "https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/_apis/public/gallery/publishers/RafaelArvelo/vsextensions/vsplotter/1.9.0/vspackage" `
  -OutFile $vsix
& "<sedea-cli>" --install-extension $vsix --force
Remove-Item -LiteralPath $vsix -Force
```

Run the probe again and require `rafaelarvelo.vsplotter@<version>` with version
≥ `1.9.0`. A download, install, or verification failure is a failed install;
route to the mission's retry/partial/abort checkpoint without inventing another
method.

